# Configuration, setup & AI backend

## `Config/AppConfig.swift`

`AppConfig` carries `appName`, `bundleId`, `backend` (`.supabase`/`.local`),
`layout` (`.list`/`.grid`), `onboardingStyle`
(`.carousel`/`.highlights`/`.minimal`), `branding` (primary/accent hex),
`featureFlags`, `legal`. `AppConfig.default` is what `DIContainer.makeDefault()`
uses at startup.

## Feature flags — `Config/FeatureFlags.swift`

**Use these exact names** (README's `enable*` names are stale).

- **Base:** `onboarding, auth, paywall, notifications, aiFeatures, appleSignIn,
  enableCaching`
- **PRO:** `charts, reviewPrompt, inAppFeedback, biometricLock, localization,
  paywallTemplates, widgets, questionnaireOnboarding, gamification, aiPro,
  camera, reminders, swiftDataStore`

The memberwise init defaults **everything to `false` except
`enableCaching = true`** — including all 13 Pro flags. `setup.sh` rewrites the
whole `featureFlags:` line. Gate both the UI and any background work behind the
flag. See `pro-features.mdc` for what each Pro flag controls.

## Secrets — `Config/Secrets.swift` (generated, gitignored)

Shape defined by `Config/Secrets.sample.swift` (compiled only with
`-D USE_SAMPLE_SECRETS`). Keys: `supabaseURL`, `supabaseAnonKey`,
`appleServiceId/appleTeamId/appleKeyId/applePrivateKeyPEM` (web SIWA only —
native iOS SIWA needs none), `accountDeletionURLString`(+`URL`),
`telemetryDeckAppID`, `revenueCatAPIKey`, `aiBackendBaseURLString`(+`URL`).

**Pro adds no new secrets** — the Gemini key lives on the server, never in the
app. **Empty keys are valid** → noop/local fallbacks. Never invent, hardcode, or
commit real values.

## Setup wizard & placeholders

`./setup.sh` (interactive) or `./setup.sh --config setup-config.json`:

- Replaces tokens repo-wide: `__APP_NAME__`, `__BUNDLE_ID__`,
  `__PRIMARY_COLOR__`, `__ACCENT_COLOR__`, `__PRIVACY_URL__`, `__TERMS_URL__`,
  `__TESTFLIGHT_APP_ID__`.
- Generates `Config/Secrets.swift`.
- Rewrites `AppConfig.swift` (`backend`, `onboardingStyle`, the full
  `featureFlags:` line **including all 13 Pro flags**) and `DesignSystem.swift`
  (`surfaceStyle`, `spacingDensity`).
- Updates `project.yml` + `project.pbxproj` and runs `xcodegen generate`.

Treat leftover `__…__` tokens as "not yet configured", not bugs — and never
commit a tree where they have already been replaced.

**If you add a feature flag, add it to `setup.sh` too**, or the wizard will
rewrite the line without it and silently drop the feature.

## XcodeGen — `project.yml`

The `.xcodeproj` is generated; **don't hand-edit it**. Two targets:

- **`TheSwiftKit`** (app, iOS 16.0) — globs `Config/`, `Core/`, `Modules/`,
  `Backend/`, `Resources/`, plus **PRO** `Widgets/Shared`.
  `Backend/Python/**` and Backend `*.md`/`*.txt` are excluded.
- **PRO `TheSwiftKitWidgets`** (`app-extension`, iOS **16.1**) — globs
  `Widgets/` (excluding its `Info.plist`), bundle id `<app>.widgets`, embedded
  in the app target.

Note `Widgets/Shared` is listed in **both** targets: Live Activity attribute
types must exist app-side and extension-side.

> **Don't "fix" the hardcoded widget bundle id.** `project.yml` ships
> `com.agaganorg.theswiftkit` (app) and `com.agaganorg.theswiftkit.widgets`
> (extension) rather than `__BUNDLE_ID__` placeholders. `setup.sh` rewrites them
> with a **global substring** replace of `com.agaganorg.theswiftkit`, so the
> widget correctly becomes `<buyer-id>.widgets` and stays prefixed by the host
> app — which app extensions require. Converting these to placeholders would
> break that.

**PRO Info.plist keys** (all commented with the feature that needs them):
`NSFaceIDUsageDescription` (AppLock), `NSCameraUsageDescription` (Capture),
`CFBundleLocalizations: [en, es, hi]` (Localization), `NSSupportsLiveActivities`
(Widgets).

Packages: Supabase 2.0.0+, TelemetryDeck SwiftSDK 1.5.1+ (product
`TelemetryClient`), RevenueCat 5.0.0+. Swift 5.9.

## AI backend — `Backend/Python/app.py` (Flask, not in the iOS target)

Keeps the provider key server-side. **PRO: dual-provider.** Set
`LLM_PROVIDER=openai` (default) or `LLM_PROVIDER=gemini` in `.env` — **the iOS
app does not change, only the server does.**

| Endpoint | OpenAI model | Gemini model | Swift caller |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/v1/chat` | `gpt-4o` | `gemini-2.5-flash` | `AIApiClient.sendChat(...)` |
| `/v1/chat/stream` **PRO** | `gpt-4o` (SSE) | `gemini-2.5-flash` (SSE) | `AIProStreamClient.stream(...)` |
| `/v1/images` | `gpt-image-1.5` | `imagen-3.0-generate-002` | `AIApiClient.generateImages(...)` |
| `/v1/vision` | `gpt-4o` | `gemini-2.5-flash` | `AIApiClient.visionAnalyze(...)` |
| `/health` | — | — | — |

Every model is env-overridable (`OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL`, `GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL`, …);
`OPENAI_BASE_URL` supports proxies/Azure. Gemini image generation needs an SDK
version exposing `ImageGenerationModel`; otherwise the server returns a clear
error suggesting `LLM_PROVIDER=openai`.

Run: `cd Backend/Python && pip install -r requirements.txt && cp .env.example
.env` (set `LLM_PROVIDER` + the matching key) `&& python app.py` (port 5001).

If you change request/response JSON, change **both** `app.py` and the Swift
`Codable` structs (`ChatReply{reply}`, `ImagesResponse{images:[String]}` base64,
`VisionResponse{result}`) so they stay in sync.

`AIProStreamClient` falls back to a built-in canned streamer when
`/v1/chat/stream` is unreachable — **keep that fallback**, it is what makes the
AI PRO demo work with no backend running.
